/// cdiesis_generics.hu - An extension of cdiesis.hu.
///
/// The original design document proposes extending a language by describing
/// the extension separately, rather than by editing the base description. This
/// file is that: applied with `hu extend`, it adds a generic type argument
/// list to the base grammar and overrides one of its constants.
///
///   hu load   "examples/hu/cdiesis.hu" g
///   hu extend "$g" "examples/hu/cdiesis_generics.hu"
///
/// The base grammar keeps its name, so a caller already holding it keeps
/// working - which is what makes this an extension rather than a replacement.

/// Override a constant the base grammar defined: a name may now be dotted.
#word IS #identifier

/// A new field, and a new alternative that reaches it.
A $declaration CAN BE $genericClass IF HAS '<'

A $genericClass HAS:
1. The $className, that IS a #word
2. The $typeArguments that ARE INSIDE '<', '>'

$typeArguments CAN HAVE ONE OR MORE $typeArgument SEPARATED BY ','
